1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,164
A salt forms when an acid reacts with a base.

2
00:00:03,164 --> 00:00:05,807
By composition there are six kinds.

3
00:00:05,807 --> 00:00:10,000
Normal salts, with every replaceable hydrogen replaced.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,179
Acid salts, like sodium bicarbonate, with some still left.

5
00:00:14,179 --> 00:00:17,343
Basic salts, with some hydroxide left.

6
00:00:17,343 --> 00:00:20,585
Double salts like Mohr's salt and potash alum.

7
00:00:20,585 --> 00:00:22,773
Mixed salts like bleaching powder.

8
00:00:22,773 --> 00:00:26,510
And complex salts like potassium ferrocyanide.

